                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "What does it mean for VPD Collection to be considered a failure?  Isn't it always just considered Completed when all the FRUs have been attempted?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/com/ibm/VPD/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 231,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "In the new approach, in case there is any failure in collecting system VPD or in case of any other major failure like system configuration load failure etc, instead of failing the service, we will let the service come up with default configurations and mark VPD collection for the system as failed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/com/ibm/VPD/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 231,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
